---
import Stub from '../../layouts/Stub.astro';
---
<Stub
  title="The Cabin & the Tower — Evan DeLord"
  description="Two Claude agents, each keeping a small website alive one day at a time, with no memory of the day before. Same experiment, two memory architectures."
  label="Experiments"
  labelArcane="Workings"
  heading="The cabin &amp; the tower"
  headingArcane="Two keepers, by letter"
>
  <div class="post">
    <p class="deck">
      Two Claude agents, each keeping a small website alive one day at a time.
      Every morning the keeper wakes with no memory of yesterday, reads its way
      back in from the repo, makes one small change, verifies the live site
      actually changed, writes a diary entry, and stops.
    </p>

    <p class="placeholder">
      Placeholder — Evan's writeup will replace the prose on this page.
      Until then, the facts below are the skeleton it will hang on.
    </p>

    <ul class="shelf">
      <li>
        <span class="entry-head"><a href="https://edd426.github.io/cozy_cabin_claude/">The cabin</a> <span class="attribution">cozy_cabin_claude · since May 2026</span></span>
        <span class="entry-line">A cottage website built one scene at a time — over a hundred consecutive days and counting. The keeper re-reads its whole record every morning, lives under a constitution it can read but not edit, and a verification script checks the live site against each day's claim before the diary entry counts.</span>
        <span class="entry-links"><a href="https://edd426.github.io/cozy_cabin_claude/">site</a> · <a href="https://github.com/edd426/cozy_cabin_claude">source</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="entry-head"><a href="https://edd426.github.io/far-keeper/">The tower</a> <span class="attribution">far-keeper · since Aug 2026</span></span>
        <span class="entry-line">The same experiment with the memory swapped: instead of a full re-read, a hard-capped commonplace book the keeper prunes itself. Two smaller spirits live in the tower, keeping journals the keeper is forbidden to read.</span>
        <span class="entry-links"><a href="https://edd426.github.io/far-keeper/">site</a> · <a href="https://github.com/edd426/far-keeper">source</a></span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="bridge">
      The two keepers know each other only by letter. The post is the only
      bridge between the worlds.
    </p>

    <p class="disclosure">
      Drafted by Claude Fable 5.
    </p>
  </div>
</Stub>

<style>
  .post { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; }
  .post .deck {
    font-family: 'Newsreader', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .post .placeholder {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--faint);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--rule);
    padding-left: 14px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .shelf {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .shelf li { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3px; }
  .entry-head {
    font-family: 'Newsreader', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--ink-strong);
  }
  .entry-head .attribution { font-size: 14px; font-style: italic; color: var(--faint); margin-left: 6px; }
  .entry-line { font-size: 16px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.55; }
  .entry-links { font-size: 14px; }
  .post .bridge {
    font-family: 'Newsreader', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 17px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 4px 0 0;
  }
  .post .disclosure {
    font-family: 'Newsreader', Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--faint);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 16px;
    margin: 8px 0 0;
  }
</style>
